N20 recurrent rollback guard for llama.cpp ec7630a640789c393694fb194f1bbbf0369fc62d (src/llama-memory-recurrent.{h,cpp} only).

llama_memory_recurrent::seq_rm accepted a rollback of r tokens whenever 1 <= r <= n_rs_seq and no rollback was
pending, without checking that snapshot plane r was written: the graph writes plane j only for j < the tokens of the
sequence in the ubatch that last wrote the cell (ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp "older slots are caller-owned"), and the
extra-row copy of build_rs rewrites plane 0 only. seq_cp left the destination's rollback index as it was, so a copy
made while the source's rollback was pending read the pre-rollback plane, and a copy into a sequence with a pending
rollback read that plane of the source's cell. Both were silent (docs/evidence/2026-10-11-n19-qwen4exp-multiseq.md
findings 5 and 6, docs/evidence/2026-10-11-n20-recurrent-rollback-guard.md).

- mem_cell::rs_n: the snapshot planes the cell's rows hold, set in find_slot (ubatch cell: min(n_seq_tokens,
  1 + n_rs_seq); extra cell: kept only if it reads its own row with no pending rollback, else 1), 1 after
  state_read.
- seq_rm: a rollback onto a plane >= rs_n returns false (logged) and changes nothing.
- seq_cp: the destination takes the source's pending rollback index (0 if the source has no cell).
- seq_rm: a rollback of a cell several sequences hold returns false, as at 79e2e74 (RC:202-205@79e2e74).

Apply to a copy, never in place: patches/llama.cpp/apply.sh <checkout at the pin> <new directory>.

